## with --src-root . (the normal way): declared Acme.Orders.Evil, sits in Acme/Evil
Acme/Evil/Evil.bs:1:1: error: `module Acme.Orders.Evil` does not match its directory
  this directory says `module Acme.Evil`
  a module's declaration and its path are the same name written
  twice, and 40 §1 makes the declaration the emitted ATOM \x{2014} so
  when they disagree the atom and the tree have drifted apart.
  Rename the directory, fix the declaration, or name the source
  root with --src-root if this tree is rooted somewhere else.
exit=1
## without --src-root (default root = the module directory's parent, Acme/):
Acme/Orders/Rules/Rules.bs:1:1: error: `module Acme.Orders.Rules` does not match its directory
  this directory says `module Rules`
  a module's declaration and its path are the same name written
  twice, and 40 §1 makes the declaration the emitted ATOM \x{2014} so
  when they disagree the atom and the tree have drifted apart.
  Rename the directory, fix the declaration, or name the source
  root with --src-root if this tree is rooted somewhere else.
exit=1
